8. **Rerun.** Rerun the step 6 command: both tests now pass.

## Tests

Both go in `crates/tools/tests/acceptance.rs`.

**`readme_the_command_table_is_the_clis`**
- Builds `let tree = cli_tree();`.
- Asserts `tree[&Vec::new()].subcommands.len() > 15`; on failure: "only {n} commands read off `jackioh -h`; clap's help format changed".
- Asserts that `tree[&vec!["promote".to_string()]].flags` has a flag named `lane` with non-empty `values`; on failure: "no possible values read off `jackioh promote -h`; clap's help format changed".
- For each `name` in `HAND_PARSED`, asserts that `tree[&vec![name.to_string()]]` has no `subcommands` and no `flags`; on failure: "`jackioh {name}` now has clap subcommands or flags: take it off HAND_PARSED so its rows are checked".
- Reads `fs::read_to_string(repo().join("crates/tools/README.md"))`, then `let usages = table_usages(&readme);`, and asserts `usages.len() > 30` (today there are 40); on failure: "…its shape changed".
- Asserts that `table_drift(&usages, &tree)` is empty; on failure: "crates/tools/README.md's command table and `jackioh` disagree (#1720): fix the row, or the CLI: {problems:#?}".

**`readme_the_drift_check_finds_each_disagreement`** (pure, no binary)
- `root = cli_command("Tools\n\nUsage: jackioh <COMMAND>\n\nCommands:\n  run      Run it\n  patches  Its own parser\n  help     Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)\n\nOptions:\n  -h, --help     Print help\n  -V, --version  Print version\n")`
  - Asserts `root.subcommands == ["run", "patches"]` and that `root.flags` is empty.
- `run = cli_command("Run it\n\nUsage: jackioh run [OPTIONS] --lane <LANE> [FILES]...\n\nArguments:\n  [FILES]...  The files\n\nOptions:\n      --lane <LANE>  The lane [default: a] [possible values: a, b, c]\n      --dry-run      Write nothing\n  -h, --help         Print help\n")`
  - Asserts its flags, as `(name, takes_value, values)`, are `("lane", true, ["a","b","c"])` and `("dry-run", false, [])`.
- `tree = BTreeMap::from([(Vec::new(), root), (vec!["run".to_string()], run), (vec!["patches".to_string()], CliCommand::default())])`.
- `drift(rows)` wraps `rows` as `format!("# x\n\n| Command | Module | Does |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n{rows}\n\nAfter.\n")` and returns `table_drift(&table_usages(&readme), &tree)`.
- `row = "| `run --lane a\\|b\\|c [--dry-run] <files>…`, `patches retcon [--any]` | `run.rs` | `run --gone`, in prose, is not read |"`.

Assert (all `assert_eq!` against these exact vectors):
- `table_usages` of the table holding `row` is `["run --lane a|b|c [--dry-run] <files>…", "patches retcon [--any]"]`.
- `drift(row)` is empty.
- With `a\\|b\\|c` replaced by `a\\|b`: ``["`jackioh run --lane c` is in no row of the table"]``.
- With `a\\|b\\|c` replaced by `a\\|b\\|c\\|d`: ``["`run --lane a|b|c|d [--dry-run] <files>…`: --lane takes no `d` (its values: a, b, c)"]``.
- With `" [--dry-run]"` replaced by `""`: ``["`jackioh run --dry-run` is in no row of the table"]``.
- With `"[--dry-run]"` replaced by `"[--dry-run] [--gone]"`: ``["`run --lane a|b|c [--dry-run] [--gone] <files>…`: `jackioh run` has no --gone"]``.
- With `` "`patches retcon [--any]`" `` replaced by `` "`patches`, `walk`" ``: ``["`walk`: `jackioh` has no subcommand `walk`"]``.
- With `` "`patches retcon [--any]`" `` replaced by `` "`run`" ``: ``["`jackioh patches` is in no row of the table"]``.

Commands:
```
cargo test -p jackioh-tools --test acceptance readme_
cargo test -p jackioh-tools
cargo clippy -p jackioh-tools --all-targets -- -D warnings
cargo fmt --check
cargo jackioh spec check
```

## Done when

- [ ] `readme_the_command_table_is_the_clis` failed at step 6 on the unedited README, `promote --lane learn` among its seven problems, and passes after step 7.
- [ ] `readme_the_drift_check_finds_each_disagreement` passes; it proves that a stale flag, a stale subcommand, a missing value and a missing command each fail.
- [ ] The README rows for trace, golden, spec and promote are corrected, and the paragraph after the table is added.
- [ ] The rest of `cargo test -p jackioh-tools` passes; V23 in particular.
- [ ] The harness's rustfmt, clippy, rulings, catalog, patches and cargo tests checks pass. No `crates/cards` change means no patch fragment.
- [ ] The PR body records the decisions under Risks.

## Risks

- **Clap help format.** A clap upgrade could change the layout of `-h`. The sanity asserts (more than 15 commands, `promote --lane` values read) make that fail loudly instead of passing empty. Always use `-h`: `--help` prints the long, multi-line form that `cli_command` cannot read.
- **V23 / `STRUCTURAL_READERS`.** Only the first cell of each table row is read, and the comment updated in step 3 says so. Do not add the Does column or the code block below the table to what is read.
- **`patches`.** It is exempt: its words and flags are hand-parsed in `patches.rs`. The `HAND_PARSED` assert fails if it ever gains a clap surface.
- **Decisions to record in the PR body:**
  1. The test parses the built binary's `-h` pages; clap introspection was rejected. The crate is bin-only, so `tests/` cannot reach `Cli::command()`. A hidden dump subcommand would add CLI surface that rule 13 then protects, and a unit test in `main.rs` would put a second Markdown reader in `src/`.
  2. CLI to table is checked for flags too, not only values. That cost three more row fixes (trace, golden, spec) and keeps a new flag from going undocumented. Rejected: checking table to CLI only.
  3. Positional placeholders are not held to clap's value names, because the README names them in its own words (`[full]` for `[BUDGET]`). Rejected: holding placeholders to clap's value names.
  4. The README's example code block is not checked. Rejected: also parsing its `cargo jackioh …` lines.

## Open questions

- `docs/v0.3.0/SURFACE.md:1067` repeats the stale `promote --lane improve|unban`. It is left alone because the issue names the README and no test reads SURFACE. A person can fix it, or file a follow-up issue for it.
